                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "64e91553-1f0f-461d-a249-595735b12a58",
                        "entry_id": "ac5e56de-e288-38e5-8a86-db5c34371a6c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "неприкоснове́нностях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0aadcfc-8e68-3657-9320-60a262438934",
                        "entry_id": "ac5e56de-e288-38e5-8a86-db5c34371a6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "свойство или состояние по значению прилагательного неприкосновенный; сохранение в целости, свобода от всякого посягательства со стороны кого-нибудь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89569000-6804-4fe0-8087-4131380306ae",
                                "sense_id": "f0aadcfc-8e68-3657-9320-60a262438934",
                                "text": "Как ни старательно утаптывали глуповцы вновь созданную плотину, как ни охраняли они её неприкосновенность в течение целой ночи, измена уже успела проникнуть в ряды их."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0a44ef3-e7de-4d29-8ee3-c042ac4ccaf4",
                                "sense_id": "f0aadcfc-8e68-3657-9320-60a262438934",
                                "text": "Неприкосновенность жилища граждан и тайна переписки охраняются законом. … Гражданам СССР обеспечивается неприкосновенность личности."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "974666bc-f825-32d3-866c-239b250783c3",
                        "entry_id": "ac5e56de-e288-38e5-8a86-db5c34371a6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "о чём-либо хорошо сохранившемся, не подвергнувшемуся какому-либо разрушительному воздействию"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "с предлогом в"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a11226af-711a-4b5f-a7a6-75f927c7ef3b",
                                "sense_id": "974666bc-f825-32d3-866c-239b250783c3",
                                "text": "В мягких толщах в изобилии попадаются бивни мамонтов, а местами даже целые трупы этих животных и их современников — длинношерстного носорога, первобытного быка, канадского оленя, лошади и многих других, — трупы, сохранившиеся в неприкосновенности, с шерстью, рогами, внутренностями, благодаря вечной мерзлоте."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2aaae3e7-d306-4687-8100-f7f56bd0a4c6",
                                "sense_id": "974666bc-f825-32d3-866c-239b250783c3",
                                "text": "Для посылки её на эту опасную планету следовало доказать, что внутри гостя далёких миров сохранились в неприкосновенности приборы и материалы, что уцелел весь обиход тех, кто вёл корабль через такие бездны пространства, перед которыми пути земных звездолётов были лишь первой робкой вылазкой в просторы космоса."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d0841b12-bbde-4d66-8f91-7efc22c75faf",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac5e56de-e288-38e5-8a86-db5c34371a6c",
                        "target_lang_word": "inviolability",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inviolability",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79f96fa6-7438-3f8c-82ab-4a71c8c3d917",
                                        "entry_id": "766db019-3b7c-3e8a-9fa9-a63d6f716553",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality or state of being inviolable; inviolableness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef9120cb-0137-4742-ab40-d29ae70f8dda",
                                                "sense_id": "79f96fa6-7438-3f8c-82ab-4a71c8c3d917",
                                                "text": "Presidential acts of forgiveness in America seldom rattle confidence in the integrity of the judicial system or the inviolability of the rule of law."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b9141a0-53c7-4c22-bdaa-b5a6518833f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac5e56de-e288-38e5-8a86-db5c34371a6c",
                        "target_lang_word": "immunity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immunity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a22d198b-e6a9-323e-8f32-fe451292f6f3",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being insusceptible to something; notably:",
                                            "Protective resistance against disease."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f3cfa13-fb60-4c9c-bdb9-2f9252130a3d",
                                                "sense_id": "a22d198b-e6a9-323e-8f32-fe451292f6f3",
                                                "text": "Some people have better immunity to diseases than others."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3eb4608d-1fde-3c88-aad3-6de0c15c160b",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being insusceptible to something; notably:",
                                            "An exemption from specified duties, such as payments or services."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a192a3b-c965-4bf0-ad9a-4350b6fdaec3",
                                                "sense_id": "3eb4608d-1fde-3c88-aad3-6de0c15c160b",
                                                "text": "Feudal privileges often included tax and other immunities."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6aef08ec-251b-3001-81f1-57512947c06f",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being insusceptible to something; notably:",
                                            "An exemption from prosecution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c299fe8-c6ee-46f2-9e46-027890e38892",
                                                "sense_id": "6aef08ec-251b-3001-81f1-57512947c06f",
                                                "text": "The prosecutor offered the lieutenant immunity for all the crimes he would testify having known to be planned by the elusive drug baron."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d32cfa04-bbe6-382e-a6ff-2b34d09540c5",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being insusceptible to something; notably:",
                                            "An exemption from penance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38abbfb2-189a-432f-a5fb-f23411eb9920",
                                                "sense_id": "d32cfa04-bbe6-382e-a6ff-2b34d09540c5",
                                                "text": "Nevertheless, his reason rebelled, and his sense of religion by no means allowed the justice of refusing the amiable, handsome, and wealthy Englishman, whom his sweet child preferred, and who was perfectly willing that the signora should enjoy all the liberty required by her conscience and her church, together with such sums as should, from time to time, purchase the prayers of the faithful, and all other immunities, so far as his fortune furnished the means."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e997c628-7f2f-3f10-afc2-be8a3f3c2bdb",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being insusceptible to something; notably:",
                                            "An exemption given to a player from losing or being withdrawn from play."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81c4bee0-9664-4413-a82a-41f8f2dca6ea",
                                                "sense_id": "e997c628-7f2f-3f10-afc2-be8a3f3c2bdb",
                                                "text": "After winning the last round the player was granted immunity which allowed him to stay in the game even after receiving the fewest points."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f5dc799-22e0-36da-a3a8-ef146c1bb9d0",
                                        "entry_id": "0aec09c5-145c-3b03-b339-5fe28743f6df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A resistance to a specific thing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78069303-b1de-45f3-9d36-f3c5d5beee83",
                                                "sense_id": "4f5dc799-22e0-36da-a3a8-ef146c1bb9d0",
                                                "text": "Superbugs are bacteria that develop an immunity to antibiotics."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
